# Stitch screens are the layout source

Before building or restyling any Attend Pal screen:

1. Call Stitch `list_screens` for project `16824782504686943603`.
2. Download that step’s screenshot and HTML with `download_file`. View them before writing code.
3. Match the Stitch layout, visible copy, spacing, and controls. Do not invent a simpler screen or paraphrase the labels.
4. Drop the Tailwind CDN, Google font links, and external image URLs. Use this repo’s design tokens and `lucide-react` (`Copy`, not `ContentCopy`).
5. Keep sample data only on Pass 1. Remove names like “Dr. Mensah” when wiring Pass 2.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — a new layout that only keeps the heading
<h1>You're marked present</h1>
<p>You can close this page.</p>

// ✅ GOOD — the Stitch screen: kiosk header, session card, chips, student row, Done
```
